# Build context for backend/Dockerfile — the Python reading service.
#
# The context has to be the repo root rather than backend/, because the trained
# models live in ML/models/ and the service resolves them as <root>/ML/models.
# That makes this file load-bearing: the root also holds 2.9 GB of things the
# image must never see.

# --- Never in an image -----------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. config.py reads .env at import, so a copy baked into the layer would
# be a real key sitting in the registry. The host supplies these as environment
# variables instead, and load_dotenv() on a missing file is a no-op.
.env
.env.*

# --- Weight ----------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/                      # 1.1 GB, and macOS wheels are wrong for linux anyway
node_modules/               # 551 MB, frontend only
.next/                      # 668 MB of build output
data set of the project/    # 354 MB of training images
aws p2 work properly/       # 257 MB, the previous deployment
data-sourse/                # 28 MB of source photography
ML/data/                    # rebuilt image dataset

# Runtime state, not build input. Uploaded cards, the vector index and the
# agent reports belong on the mounted volume, not in the image — baking them in
# would ship one machine's uploads to every deploy.
backend/data/

# --- Not the service -------------------------------------------------------
src/
public/
.git/
.github/
.idea/
.claude/
*.ipynb
tsconfig*.json
next.config.ts
postcss.config.mjs
eslint.config.mjs
package*.json

# --- Noise -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
